        "readable_text": "Content:\nRecall that the absolute value of a number represents the distance of that number from the origin.\n\nContent:\nLet's take a look at the number line below.\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/1d951cedd50f792b48ebac86ff6d6fe2]\n\nContent:\nSince [MATH: -3] and [MATH: 3] are at the same distance from the origin, we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |-3| = |3| = 3.]\n\nContent:\nIn general, for any real number [MATH: a,]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |-a| = |a|.]\n\nContent:\nWe can use this fact to simplify expressions containing absolute value. Let's see an example."
