      {
        "lesson_index": 5,
        "step_index": 3,
        "item_type": "step",
        "step_type": "tutorial",
        "step_id": "36686",
        "content_id": "6011",
        "dom_id": "step-36686",
        "selector": "#step-36686",
        "step_anchor": "step-5",
        "title": "The Distributive Properties",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The absolute value operation is <strong>distributive with respect to multiplication.</strong> This means that the absolute value of a product equals the product of the absolute values.</p>",
            "readable_text": "The absolute value operation is distributive with respect to multiplication. This means that the absolute value of a product equals the product of the absolute values.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To demonstrate, consider the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "To demonstrate, consider the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |(-6) \\cdot 2|]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |(-6) \\cdot 2|]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can evaluate this expression in two separate ways:</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can evaluate this expression in two separate ways:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p>The first is to find the absolute value of the product. In doing this, we get</p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- The first is to find the absolute value of the product. In doing this, we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 12|; = 12.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 12|; = 12.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p>The second is to find the product of the absolute values. In doing this, we get</p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- The second is to find the product of the absolute values. In doing this, we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 6|\u22c5|2|; = 6 \u22c5 2; = 12.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 6|\u22c5|2|; = 6 \u22c5 2; = 12.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In general</p>",
            "readable_text": "In general",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |a \\cdot b| = |a|\\cdot |b|.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: |a \\cdot b| = |a|\\cdot |b|.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The absolute value operation is also distributive with respect to division. In general,</p>",
            "readable_text": "The absolute value operation is also distributive with respect to division. In general,",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThe absolute value operation is distributive with respect to multiplication. This means that the absolute value of a product equals the product of the absolute values.\n\nContent:\nTo demonstrate, consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(-6) \\cdot 2|]\n\nContent:\nWe can evaluate this expression in two separate ways:\n\nContent:\n- The first is to find the absolute value of the product. In doing this, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 12|; = 12.]\n\nContent:\n- The second is to find the product of the absolute values. In doing this, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 6|\u22c5|2|; = 6 \u22c5 2; = 12.]\n\nContent:\nIn general\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |a \\cdot b| = |a|\\cdot |b|.]\n\nContent:\nThe absolute value operation is also distributive with respect to division. In general,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}.]"
      },
