            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Firstly, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: |-a| = |a|,]</span> we can write our expression as</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.]</span></p><p>Then, we distribute the absolute value over the division, and simplify:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: |(9)/(5c)||=; (|9|)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5|\u22c5|c|)|=; (9)/(5|c|)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Firstly, since [MATH: |-a| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the division, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: |(9)/(5c)||=; (|9|)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5|\u22c5|c|)|=; (9)/(5|c|)]",
            "images": [],
