    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nRecall that the absolute value of a number represents the distance of that number from the origin.\n\nContent:\nLet's take a look at the number line below.\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/1d951cedd50f792b48ebac86ff6d6fe2]\n\nContent:\nSince [MATH: -3] and [MATH: 3] are at the same distance from the origin, we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |-3| = |3| = 3.]\n\nContent:\nIn general, for any real number [MATH: a,]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |-a| = |a|.]\n\nContent:\nWe can use this fact to simplify expressions containing absolute value. Let's see an example.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Simplifying the Absolute Value of a Negative Term\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: |-2x|.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nSince [MATH: |-a| = |a|,] we can rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n[MATH: |\u2212 2x||=|2x|]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |\u2212 4x|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 4]\nb. [MATH: \u2212|4x|]\nc. [MATH: |4x|]\nd. [MATH: 4]\ne. [MATH: 16x]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |\u2212 (4z)/(7)|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (4)/(7)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212|(4z)/(7)|]\nc. [MATH: |(4z)/(7)|]\nd. [MATH: (4)/(7)]\ne. [MATH: |(4)/(7)|]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: The Distributive Properties\n\nContent:\nThe absolute value operation is distributive with respect to multiplication. This means that the absolute value of a product equals the product of the absolute values.\n\nContent:\nTo demonstrate, consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(-6) \\cdot 2|]\n\nContent:\nWe can evaluate this expression in two separate ways:\n\nContent:\n- The first is to find the absolute value of the product. In doing this, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 12|; = 12.]\n\nContent:\n- The second is to find the product of the absolute values. In doing this, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |(\u2212 6) \u22c5 2||=|\u2212 6|\u22c5|2|; = 6 \u22c5 2; = 12.]\n\nContent:\nIn general\n\nContent:\n[MATH: |a \\cdot b| = |a|\\cdot |b|.]\n\nContent:\nThe absolute value operation is also distributive with respect to division. In general,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Distributing the Absolute Value Over Multiplication\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: |-18a|.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirstly, since [MATH: |-a| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: |18a|]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: |18a||=;|18 \u22c5 a||=;|18|\u22c5|a||=; 18 \u22c5|a||=; 18|a|]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |5x|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212|5x|]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 5]\nc. [MATH: 5]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 5|x|]\ne. [MATH: 5|x|]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: |\u2212 11x|.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212|11x|]\nb. [MATH: 11]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 11|x|]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 11]\ne. [MATH: 11|x|]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Distributing the Absolute Value Over Division\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: \\left|-\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirstly, since [MATH: |-a| = |a|,] we can write our expression as\n\n[MATH: \\left|\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.]\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the division, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: |(9)/(5c)||=; (|9|)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5c|)|=; (9)/(|5|\u22c5|c|)|=; (9)/(5|c|)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: |\u2212 (3)/(2x)|=]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (3)/(2|x|)]\nb. [MATH: 6x]\nc. [MATH: (3)/(2)]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (3)/(2|x|)]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 6x]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify the expression [MATH: |\u2212 (5x)/(3y)|.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (5|x|)/(3|y|)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 15xy]\nc. [MATH: 15xy]\nd. [MATH: (5|x|)/(3|y|)]\ne. [MATH: (5)/(3)]"
  }
